@startuml
' Context diagram at the level of the Components-and-Connectors view (Figure 6).
' Authored in Slice 2. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
!include style.puml
title Components-and-Connectors view: context diagram

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Store\nmanager" as SM
actor "DC\nmanager" as DM
node "External\nPOS system\n(per store)" as POS #6FA8DC
node "External Analytics\nClient (future\nsubscriber)" as ANLY #6FA8DC

rectangle "**Supermarket Inventory Tracking System**\n(stores + distribution center;\nscope of this C&C view)" as SYS #93C47D

POS --> SYS : <<event stream>>\nsales records
SYS --> ANLY : <<pub-sub>>\ninventory events
SYS --> SM : <<request/reply>>\nstore inventory views
SM --> SYS : <<request/reply>>\nlocal queries, order confirmation
SYS --> DM : <<request/reply>>\nmaster inventory,\nreports, shipping orders
DM --> SYS : <<request/reply>>\nqueries

legend bottom
  The shaded box is the view's scope: the store systems and the
  distribution-center system of the primary presentation, taken as one.
  Blue boxes are external systems: the POS system feeds a one-way event
  stream in, and the External Analytics Client is an external subscriber.
  Stick figures are human roles. The n-ary <<pub-sub>>, <<data access>>
  and <<local call>> connectors are internal to the box.
endlegend
@enduml
